WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.000
Anthropic, the company behind Claude, has filed to go public.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.080
Ticker: ANT, on the Nasdaq.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.410
An IPO is the first time a private company sells shares to the public.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.410
After that, anyone can trade them on the exchange.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.200
Revenue: $16.3 billion in the first half of 2026,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.190
and a reported $16.8 billion in the third quarter alone.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.980
The expectation: raise about $100 billion at a valuation of up to $2 trillion.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.490
That would be the largest IPO in history.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.800
SpaceX set the record in June: $75 billion raised, shares up 19% on day one.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:46.220
Anthropic amended its filing on November 2. Trading is reported for around November 20.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:56.500
And NVIDIA? The amended filing shows nearly $900 billion of computing commitments, with NVIDIA as Anthropic's largest chip supplier.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:02.760
Chip stocks rose on the filing, and NVIDIA may take a stake of about $10 billion in the IPO.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:08.940
But Anthropic also buys from Google, Amazon and AMD. A demand signal, not a guarantee.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.650
The share price is not set yet.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.100
It comes in a further amended filing just before trading.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.160
Watch the official price range, and the first day of trading.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.380
Shares are highly speculative. This is information, not advice.
